  "worked_solution": "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(4\\,|\\,1)=P(X=4\\,|\\,Y=1).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=4\\,|\\,Y=1)=\\frac{P(X=4,Y=1)}{P(Y=1)}=\\frac{f(4,1)}{{f}_{Y}(1)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(1) & =f(2,1)+f(4,1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{27}+\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(4,1)=\\frac{1}{9}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{Y}(1)=\\frac{8}{27}$ and $f(4,1)=\\frac{1}{9}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(4\\,|\\,1) & =P(X=4\\,|\\,Y=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(4,1)}{{f}_{Y}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{9})}{(\\frac{8}{27})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
